Icon sets ("skins") for the Xymon pages. Each directory is one set, with a
skin.json that says what it holds:

    {"type": "svg", "icons": ["green", "green-recent", ...], "static": ["red", ...]}

"type" is the files' extension, "icons" the names the set has, and "static"
the names that also have a still variant in static/, used when moving icons
are switched off. index.json lists the sets the Look and feel page offers;
"text" there is the set drawn in characters, which needs no files.

classic: the icons of Xymon itself, from xymond/wwwfiles/gifs in the Xymon
    source. Copyright (C) Henrik Storner and the Xymon contributors.
accessible: every colour has its own shape as well as its own colour, in
    the Okabe-Ito palette, so a status can be told apart without colour
    vision.
vector: flat icons, a different symbol for each colour; a recent change is
    a face.

accessible and vector: Copyright (C) 2026 Stef Coene.

